WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.110
24 October 1970.

2
00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:07.490
A UN resolution takes up a target
for the world's richer countries.

3
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:12.470
They should give 0.7 per cent of
their gross national income as aid.

4
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:18.190
Aid can be money, goods or expertise,
given or lent to poorer countries.

5
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.070
More than fifty years on,
very few keep that promise.

6
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:22.950
Why?

7
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.830
Can they really not afford it?

8
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.410
In this mission, you'll
sort the main types of aid,

9
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.610
and the deals governments
make to narrow the gap.

10
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.010
Then you'll test the
target against real data,

11
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.450
and weigh up different views.

12
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:41.480
Your mission: explain why so few rich
countries keep the 0.7 per cent promise.
